BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T150000
UID:6a2748dd72ddb73600808e5e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA Writers Collective of Canada (WCC) workshop is unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect. (wcc-cec.org)\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. 
 Materials are provided.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Third Floor\, Discussion Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2748dd72ddb73600808e5e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T150000
UID:6a4c0e2a86636e3d00530816@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us to discuss books in a fun\, friendly and welcoming env
 ironment. New members are always welcome!\nComing Up at Book Club: “\nTh
 e woman in the window\n" by "A.J.Finn"\nNo registration required.
LOCATION:Thorncliffe
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4c0e2a86636e3d00530816
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Writing For Newcomers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T143000
UID:6a516f350d65ac36003eded0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program provides a supportive\, low-pressure environment 
 where newcomers can build confidence in their English writing\, communicat
 ion\, and presentation skills. Together\, we will:\n1. Have a short\, coll
 ective discussion period.\n2. Begin writing based on a prompt from the ins
 tructor\n(Example: This year\, I learned... Last week\, I did... Something
  funny happened when…)\n3. Present what we wrote to the group.\nPlease n
 ote: This is a group meeting. We do not offer individual lessons. We will 
 not be spell-checking\, looking at punctuation\, grammar\, ect. We will be
  focusing on basic sentence structure and presentation.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Activity Room (Youth Hub\, First Floo
 r)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a516f350d65ac36003eded0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
